Dear all

I am having some problems creating a PCA plot using colored symbols. When I used the function pch to determine the shape of the point, I am finding that the function is deleting numerous data points from the plot.

For example, when I used this line below I have around 270 points on my plot:
plot(PCA$pc.scores[,1], PCA$pc.scores[,2], pch=21, bg=classifier, col=gray.colors(7), cex=0.8, xlab=xlab, ylab=ylab, main = "title",cex.main=0.8,cex.axis=0.8,cex.lab=0.8,font.lab=2)

when I add in the pch function I find that many of my points disappear and some of the points suddenly change to a new classifier:
plot(PCA$pc.scores[,1], PCA$pc.scores[,2], pch=c(21:25,15,4), bg=classifier, col=gray.colors(7), cex=0.8, xlab=xlab, ylab=ylab, main = "title",cex.main=0.8,cex.axis=0.8,cex.lab=0.8,font.lab=2)

I am struggling to understand what I could be doing wrong. Any advice would be greatly appreciated! Thank you.

